50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Ledger Bridge offers the independent verification I like, but it's software. Clinic Scheduler and Harvest Sensor would complicate my audits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Clinic Scheduler and Harvest Sensor have the retention profiles I prefer. Ledger Bridge fits the profile of our previous successful exits.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor involve physical stock or hardware, which helps with the credit line but risks high follow-on calls.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mio,,I can't do more software. Ledger Bridge and Clinic Scheduler are out. Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor fit our idle advisers.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Clinic Scheduler will be stuck in security review for months. Harvest Sensor and Fabric Loop risk supply chain or staffing delays.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Mio, if you can't handle more software, Ledger Bridge is out, despite the reporting benefits.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, is Ledger Bridge's security review as bad as the medical one? If not, it's the most logical win.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, Ledger Bridge is a subscription model. We can't borrow against it. Fabric Loop's resale channel might be better for liquidity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Minako, but Fabric Loop needs shift supervisors! My recruiters can't find them. Harvest Sensor is a better middle ground.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Harvest Sensor has hardware risks, but Ledger Bridge is a ""safe"" software bet that avoids the medical security nightmare.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I'm leaning toward Ledger Bridge. The reporting is clean, and it avoids the audit fees of depots and sensors.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. It matches our exit history and avoids the medical delays Toshio mentioned.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I still worry about the credit line, but Ledger Bridge is the leanest option. It won't drain reserves like a warehouse would.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I really hate the idea of more software board seats, but I see the point about the staffing nightmare for the others.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Ledger Bridge is the most predictable deployment. No medical records, no physical controllers to wait for.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,It seems we have a consensus on Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for Ledger Bridge.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'll go with Ledger Bridge, though I'm not happy about the board seats.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Ledger Bridge it is.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
